To configure your Nokia 7750 SR routers to advertise only the single best path per prefix to BGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    no advertise-inactive
    no advertise-external
```

### Explanation:
1. **`no advertise-inactive`**:  
   Ensures only the active best path (selected by the route table manager) is advertised. Disabling this prevents inactive routes from being propagated.

2. **`no advertise-external`**:  
   Disables the advertisement of external paths when the best overall route is internal. This guarantees only one path (the absolute best) is shared per prefix.

These commands enforce the default BGP behavior of advertising a single best path, streamlining your routing tables without disrupting legitimate route propagation. If `advertise-inactive` or `advertise-external` was previously enabled at the group or neighbor level, apply `no advertise-inactive` there as well for consistency.
