To implement a syslog warning when receiving around 5,000 IPv6 routes without disrupting the BGP session, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <your-group-name>
        family ipv6
        neighbor <neighbor-IP>
            prefix-limit ipv6 5000 threshold 80 log-only
```

### Key elements:
- `prefix-limit ipv6 5000`: Sets the IPv6 route limit to 5,000
- `threshold 80`: Triggers the warning at 4,000 routes (80% of 5,000)
- `log-only`: Ensures only syslog warnings are generated (no session teardown)

